libhybris: don't call bionic's __system_properties_init when there is no property area

The hybris linker deliberately skips libc.so's constructors, but it makes one
exception: it dlsyms bionic's real __system_properties_init() out of the loaded
libc.so and calls it, so that Android libraries can read properties.

On a device where Android's init never runs, /dev/__properties__ does not exist,
and that call dereferences NULL. Confirmed by strace on sol (Pixel Watch 3,
Android 14 system libs, no Android userspace):

    openat(AT_FDCWD, "/dev/cpu_variant:arm", O_RDONLY) = -1 ENOENT
    openat(AT_FDCWD, "/dev/__properties__", O_RDONLY|...) = -1 ENOENT
    --- SIGSEGV {si_signo=SIGSEGV, si_code=SEGV_MAPERR, si_addr=0x410} ---

Creating the directory is not enough; bionic then reads the SELinux property
context files (which do exist) and goes looking for the per-context area:

    openat(AT_FDCWD, "/system/etc/selinux/plat_property_contexts", ...) = 3
    openat(AT_FDCWD, "/vendor/etc/selinux/vendor_property_contexts", ...) = 3
    openat(AT_FDCWD, "/dev/__properties__/properties_serial", ...) = -1 ENOENT
    --- SIGSEGV ... si_addr=0x410 ---

A correctly populated property area is something Android's init builds; a
libhybris-only system has no way to produce one, and does not need one, because
libhybris already serves property reads through its own __system_property_*
hooks (that is exactly why the hook table has them).

So make the call conditional on an area actually being present. Where one exists
-- for instance on ports that run an Android container, which is where this code
path has always worked -- behaviour is unchanged. Where one does not, the linker
now proceeds instead of taking the process down at load time.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/common/q/linker_soinfo.cpp
+++ b/common/q/linker_soinfo.cpp
@@ -447,12 +447,22 @@
 
   if (soname_ != nullptr && strcmp(soname_, "libc.so") == 0) {
     DEBUG("HYBRIS: =============> Skipping libc.so (but initializing properties)\n");
-    bionic___system_properties_init = (void(*)())android_dlsym(this, "__system_properties_init");
-    if (!bionic___system_properties_init) {
-        fprintf(stderr, "Could not initialize android system properties!\n");
-        abort();
+    // Only hand control to bionic's property-area initialiser if an area
+    // actually exists. Without Android's init there is none, and bionic
+    // dereferences NULL (SIGSEGV at 0x410) before we ever reach main().
+    // libhybris serves property reads via its own __system_property_* hooks,
+    // so skipping this costs nothing on such a system.
+    if (access("/dev/__properties__/properties_serial", R_OK) == 0) {
+        bionic___system_properties_init = (void(*)())android_dlsym(this, "__system_properties_init");
+        if (!bionic___system_properties_init) {
+            fprintf(stderr, "Could not initialize android system properties!\n");
+            abort();
+        }
+        bionic___system_properties_init();
+    } else {
+        DEBUG("HYBRIS: no bionic property area (/dev/__properties__), "
+              "skipping __system_properties_init; hybris hooks serve properties\n");
     }
-    bionic___system_properties_init();
     constructors_called = true;
     return;
   }
